WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.463
Where shooting stars come from.

00:03.163 --> 00:07.058
A comet leaves a trail of dusty debris along its path.

00:07.508 --> 00:14.698
Where the Earth passes through one, the dust hits our air at tens of thousands of kilometres an hour and burns up.

00:15.148 --> 00:18.779
Most of the pieces are between a grain of sand and a pea.

00:19.229 --> 00:22.850
That is a meteor shower, and it comes back every year.
